{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547176-idiosynchratic-spell-effects","id":1547176,"title":"Idiosynchratic spell effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-21T10:00:30-08:00","id":1547176,"title":"Idiosynchratic spell effects","content":"What spheres are needed in your opinion to make Idiosynchratic effects --&gt; Cause things that typically make people react in certain ways.<br /> A good example here would be to affect the sense of touch to cause pain (but no damage) to the hand of the target carrying a weapon to make him drop it.<br /> How would you judge such an intent in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T13:51:29-08:00","id":1547179,"title":"","content":"That's an immense category of potential effects. Almost every Sphere has at least some application towards &quot;make people react in certain ways.&quot;<br /> <br /> When it comes to running the game, one of the main things I discuss with players that are coming up with effects on the fly, is what is their goal. In your example, is the goal to cause &quot;touch = pain,&quot; and touching weapons becoming a no-go a bonus, or is their goal to get an opponent to change their mind when reaching for a weapon after forming the intent to draw said weapon? Because those are different goals with different implications. Knowing what the core effect they're trying to accomplish is always the most important part because even if their thoughts on Spheres and my thoughts on Spheres aren't aligned, we can discuss different options, and find the best Spheres that their character possesses to produce an effect as close as possible to their core intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T22:31:51-08:00","id":1547182,"title":"","content":"It's a very general question, and often there is more than one way of accomplishing a given effect using magick.<br /> <br /> Most often, Mind effects are involved when messing with the senses of other people, or creating overriding impulses. The section on Uncanny Influence in How Do You DO That has some pretty good advice on dealing with this, in the subsection on creating illusions. <i>If </i>a mage knows exactly what he's doing, Life can produce some similar effects, but that depends on the mage having enough knowledge of things like the human nervous system and/or how muscles function. This is also described in the section entitled Tweaking Chemistry. These sections also explain how a target might resist these sorts of effects, and how the stats of the target can determine the casting difficulty.<br /> <br /> Using your example, one might use a Mind Effect to create illusory pain in the hand and/or an immediate impulse to drop the firearm. On the other hand, one might also use Life to cause either a brief but intense bit of &quot;idiopathic&quot; pain in the hand, and/or induce a muscle spasm.<br /> <br /> Either of these might very well be coincidental effects, as people do experience annoying twinges and muscle spasms. Unless the Hypothetical Omniscient Observer is constantly scanning the whole of humanity with one huge MRI and performing other advanced neurological monitoring on everyone, it'd be pretty difficult to argue the vulgarity of it. A Hypothetical Average Bystander certainly isn't likely to think anything of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-22-2024, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T12:07:46-08:00","id":1547189,"title":"","content":"It's important to note that either Hypothetical is not necessary if there's an actual witness to something supernatural by the mage. Shared supernatural senses with Sleepers is usually vulgar without some work from the mage to frame things because there's a direct witness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T16:08:24-08:00","id":1547192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547176-idiosynchratic-spell-effects?p=1547189#post1547189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to note that either Hypothetical is not necessary if there's an actual witness to something supernatural by the mage. Shared supernatural senses with Sleepers is usually vulgar without some work from the mage to frame things because there's a direct witness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, overriding the sensory perceptions of a Sleeper such that they will share your Awakened senses is generally vulgar, unless that Sleeper is already in some unusual mental state in which they're expecting to experience things which are out of the ordinary. If the fuzz on your tongue is tickling your brain, and you've discovered that you can breathe in stereo, your suspension of disbelief is already fully engaged and you're ready to listen to the music of the Spheres and see all the pretty aura colors and underlying patterns of the cosmos. That's all covered un HDYDT, in the section on Enhanced Perceptions.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, mental illusions are coincidental by default, unless the mage does something truly absurd to make it very clear that they're the cause of said illusions. Even then, if the tools and methods said mage is using make it <i>plausible </i>that the subject is going to experience something unusual as a result, it can still be coincidental. If that Ecstatic has passed you a hit of whatever they've been smoking, and you graciously accept, they can send you on a brief trip to Wonderland without any hassle from Consensus.<br /> <br /> When it comes to &quot;external&quot; illusions, generally ones created with Forces effects which are perceptible to anyone in the vicinity, the litmus test is apparent believability. (&quot;Apparent&quot; being used in the most literal sense here.) If what that illusion appears to be would not defy belief, then it's coincidental. If it <i>does </i>defy what observers consider possible, then it's vulgar.<br /> <br /> The above is a brief summary taken from HDYDT, specifically the section on Uncanny Influence. The Arts of Illusion subsection goes into a good bit more detail on all of this, and is very relevant to what the original poster was asking after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-26-2024, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}